---
code: dorc-sh-no-shell
when-fires: dorc-sh resolved no POSIX shell through the one-shell-answer seat (dorc_transport::Posix::find), so it refuses before running the stripped script. cli/bin/dorc-sh.rs.
why: on native Windows a bare `sh` PATH lookup finds `%SystemRoot%\System32\bash.exe`, the WSL launcher, not a POSIX shell; resolving through the seat and refusing loudly when git's userland is absent is the difference between an actionable 'install git' and a silent wrong-shell run. Remediation register (help) wanted.
---
-- webhost.sh --
#!/bin/sh
true

-- edge-fault --
shim-no-shell

-- replay --
$ dorc-sh webhost.sh
dorc-sh: error[dorc-sh-no-shell]: [unwritten: dorc-sh-no-shell]
